Markup Shorthands: markdown on
Boilerplate: omit style-colors, omit style-dfn-panel, omit style-ref-hints, omit style-issues, omit style-selflinks, omit style-counters, omit style-autolinks, omit style-md-lists, omit script-dom-helper, omit script-dfn-panel, omit script-ref-hints
Abstract: Tests inline vs block classification and serialization of math elements.
</pre>

<math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> starts a paragraph by default.

Paragraph continued by
<math><mi>y</mi></math> on the next line.

<math display=inline><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math> starts a paragraph when inline.

Paragraph continued by
<math display=inline><mi>z</mi></math> on the next line.

<math display=block><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>

Paragraph interrupted by block math:
<math display=block><mi>k</mi></math>

<div>Inline container with <math><mi>x</mi></math> and <math display=inline><mi>y</mi></math> stays inline.</div>

<div>Mixed container with <math display=block><mi>z</mi></math> splits into blocks.</div>
